{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":26630,"name":"","username":"ArthurZhang","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/arthurzhang/{size}/11070_2.png","created_at":"2026-10-13T15:03:10.602Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eDuring a brainstorming session with Matt, Shawn, Leigh, Yukun and a few others, I brought up an idea that I think could be worth exploring.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe have quite a few promising projects and talented developers across the CKB ecosystem, but many of them are working in relative isolation. Sometimes two teams are solving closely related problems without knowing it. Other times, a project needs precisely the expertise that somebody elsewhere in the community already has.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat if we built a platform that continuously looks for these connections?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet’s call it \u003cstrong\u003eProject Matchmaker\u003c/strong\u003e for now. This is just a brainstorming proposal, not an agreed roadmap.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-26630-the-product-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-26630-the-product-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eThe product\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImagine a shared directory of developers, projects, repositories and ongoing research, with a few AI agents working behind the scenes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDevelopers could register their skills, interests, availability and preferred areas of contribution. Projects could describe what they’re building, their dependencies, outstanding problems and where they need help.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe agents would then analyse potential synergies across the ecosystem and produce a daily or weekly collaboration report.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor example:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProject A has developed a reusable ZK verification component that Project B could integrate.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProject C needs someone familiar with CKB transaction composition, while Developer D has recently been working on precisely that.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTwo teams are implementing similar infrastructure and might benefit from sharing a library rather than maintaining separate implementations.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA newly announced project has architectural dependencies or research interests that overlap with three existing teams.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen a new project makes its debut, the platform could automatically generate a short \u003cstrong\u003ecollaboration opportunity report\u003c/strong\u003e, suggesting relevant developers, existing projects, reusable components and potential contributors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-26630-possible-architecture-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-26630-possible-architecture-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003ePossible architecture\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI imagine a relatively straightforward system built around a continuously updated knowledge graph.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1. Discovery layer:\u003c/strong\u003e Collect information from public GitHub repositories, issues, Nervos Talk discussions and voluntarily submitted developer/project profiles. Private community data would require explicit permission.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e2. Knowledge graph:\u003c/strong\u003e Represent developers, projects, skills, protocol components, dependencies and open problems as connected entities, with links back to supporting evidence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e3. Agent layer:\u003c/strong\u003e Run specialised agents for project discovery, technical capability analysis, collaboration matching and opportunity reporting. Matching could combine semantic search with graph relationships, rather than relying entirely on an LLM’s judgement.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e4. Product layer:\u003c/strong\u003e A searchable community directory, project onboarding, personalised collaboration suggestions and a regular ecosystem synergy digest.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportantly, every recommendation should explain \u003cem\u003ewhy\u003c/em\u003e two parties might benefit from working together, with links to actual code, issues or research. People should be able to correct recommendations, decline introductions and control their own availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ethis is purely a brainstorm\u003c/strong\u003e. I’d love to hear whether people think this would actually be useful, what existing tools we could build upon, and whether anyone would be interested in experimenting with a prototype.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-10-13T15:03:10.602Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":26.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":10992,"topic_slug":"brainstorm-project-matchmaker-an-agent-assisted-collaboration-network-for-the-ckb-ecosystem","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"Newbie","title_is_group":false,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4255,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/brainstorm-project-matchmaker-an-agent-assisted-collaboration-network-for-the-ckb-ecosystem/10992/1","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_